{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"curl -L -sS 'https://zenodo.org/api/records/10000430/files/README.md/content'\"","aggregated_output":"# CLUSTER RNAseq deconvolution project 2023\n\nFive datasets are uploaded and listed in the table below.\n\n\t    fileName                             Description\n\t-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\t1 | Sample_annotated_Zenodo.csv        | Sample annotation\n\t2 | RawReadCounts_Zenodo.csv           | Raw read count matrix\n\t3 | BatchCorrectedReadCounts_Zenodo.csv| Batch-corrected read count matrix\n\t4 | GeneMetaInfo_Zenodo.csv            | Gene Information\n\t5 | FlowSorterFraction_Zenodo.csv      | Cell type fractions\n\n## Description of the data and file structure\n\n**Sample_annotated_Zenodo.csv**\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThere are 723 rows (samples) and 6 columns in this file. Definitions of\ncolumn variables are explained in the following.\n\n- **sample**: sample names used in read count matrices\n\n- **samp**: subject Id\n\n- **samtype**: refsamp for training samples; nonrefsamp for testing\n  samples\n\n- **cell type**: PBMC, CD4, CD8, CD14, CD19\n\n- **batch**: RNAseq sequencing batch\n\n- **sex**: M for male; F for female\n\nThe first 3 rows of this dataset are shown below.\n\n           sample   samp samtype celltype batch sex\n    1:  CHC096CD4 CHC096 refsamp      CD4     1   M\n    2:  CHC096CD8 CHC096 refsamp      CD8     1   M\n    3: CHC096CD14 CHC096 refsamp     CD14     1   M\n\n**RawReadCounts_Zenodo.csv**\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nRaw read count matrix (59453 genes \\* 723 samples). **Gene’s name is the\nfirst column without a header (column name)**. featureCount was used to summarise read\ncounts based on Homo_sapiens.GRCh38.103.gtf.\n\nRead counts of the first 5 genes for the first 6 samples are shown\nbelow.\n\n                CHC096CD4 CHC096CD8 CHC096CD14 CHC096CD19 CHC096PBMC THC040CD4\n    DDX11L1           247       255        128        167        214        38\n    WASH7P          10377      8277       6570       7641       6263      2890\n    MIR6859-1         229       199         94         84         70        34\n    MIR1302-2HG         3         0          3          1          0         0\n    MIR1302-2           0         0          0          0          0         0\n\n**BatchCorrectedReadCounts_Zenodo.csv**\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nBatch-corrected read count matrix (59453 genes \\* 723 samples) derived\nusing\n[Combat-Seq](https://academic.oup.com/nargab/article/2/3/lqaa078/5909519).\n**Gene’s name is the first column without a header (column name).**\n\nBatch-corrected read counts of the first 5 genes for the first 6 samples\nare shown below.\n\n                CHC096CD4 CHC096CD8 CHC096CD14 CHC096CD19 CHC096PBMC THC040CD4\n    DDX11L1           175       182         90        117        152        27\n    WASH7P           6463      5144       4251       4916       4022      1882\n    MIR6859-1         143       123         68         62         52        26\n    MIR1302-2HG         3         0          4          1          0         0\n    MIR1302-2           0         0          0          0          0         0\n\n**GeneMetaInfo_Zenodo.csv**\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nInformation on gene name (**Geneid**), chromosome (**Chr**), gene length\n(**Length**), gene type (**gene_biotype**) for 59453 genes (rows).\n**Gene’s name is the first column without a header (column name).**\n\nThe first 3 rows of this dataset are shown below.\n\n                 Geneid Chr Length                       gene_biotype\n    DDX11L1     DDX11L1   1   1735 transcribed_unprocessed_pseudogene\n    WASH7P       WASH7P   1   1351             unprocessed_pseudogene\n    MIR6859-1 MIR6859-1   1     68                              miRNA\n\n**FlowSorterFraction_Zenodo.csv**\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nOrganised by PBMC sample names of subjects (rows) and cell types\n(columns). Cell type fractions were derived from flow sorter data. For each subject, we divided CD4, CD8, CD14, and CD19 cell counts by the sum of CD4, CD8, CD14 and CD19 cells to obtain cell-type fractions.\n\n\nThe first 3 rows of this dataset are shown below.\n\n                     CD4       CD8      CD14      CD19\n    CHC096PBMC 0.4269334 0.2493598 0.1552741 0.1684327\n    THC040PBMC 0.4951259 0.2367423 0.1413210 0.1268107\n    CHC177PBMC 0.4745677 0.2221926 0.1956962 0.1075434\n\n## Code/Software\n\n- Raw read counts were generated using\n  [RSSnextflow](https://gitlab.com/b8307038/rssnextflow), customised\n  pipeline for UMI-tagged RNAseq data.\n\n- These datasets were utilised in the [imputation of cell-type\n  expression workflow](https://gitlab.com/b8307038/deconvimpvexpr) for\n  this preprint-[Imputation of cell-type specific expression using\n  RNA-seq data from mixed cell\n  populations](https://doi.org/10.1101/2023.09.11.556650).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport csv, math\n# read sample annotations with csv\ncd14=set()\nwith open('inputs/Sample_annotated_Zenodo.csv', newline='') as f:\n    r=csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in r:\n        if row['celltype']=='CD14':\n            cd14.add(row['sample'])\nprint('n cd14', len(cd14))\n# read meta\nlength={}; biotype={}\nwith open('inputs/GeneMetaInfo_Zenodo.csv', newline='') as f:\n    r=csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in r:\n        length[row['Geneid']]=float(row['Length'])\n        biotype[row['Geneid']]=row['gene_biotype']\n# stream count matrix, compute total and mean for protein_coding only\nwith open('inputs/BatchCorrectedReadCounts_Zenodo.csv', newline='') as f:\n    r=csv.DictReader(f)\n    headers=r.fieldnames\n    cols=[i for i,h in enumerate(headers) if h in cd14]\n    print('cd14 cols found', len(cols))\n    totals=[]; means=[]; lens=[]; genes=[]\n    for row in r:\n        gene=row[headers[0]]\n        if biotype.get(gene)=='protein_coding':\n            s=0.0\n            for i in cols:\n                val=row[headers[i]]\n                s += float(val)\n            if s>=10:\n                n=len(cols)\n                totals.append(s)\n                means.append(s/n)\n                lens.append(length[gene])\n                genes.append(gene)\nprint('eligible', len(totals))\n# Pearson pure\nn=len(lens)\nmx=sum(lens)/n; my=sum(means)/n\nsxy=sum((lens[i]-mx)*(means[i]-my) for i in range(n))\nsxx=sum((lens[i]-mx)**2 for i in range(n))\nsyy=sum((means[i]-my)**2 for i in range(n))\nr=sxy/math.sqrt(sxx*syy)\nprint('r pure', repr(r))\nprint('meanx', mx, 'meany', my)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport csv, math\n# read sample annotations with csv\ncd14=set()\nwith open('inputs/Sample_annotated_Zenodo.csv', newline='') as f:\n    r=csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in r:\n        if row['celltype']=='CD14':\n            cd14.add(row['sample'])\nprint('n cd14', len(cd14))\n# read meta\nlength={}; biotype={}\nwith open('inputs/GeneMetaInfo_Zenodo.csv', newline='') as f:\n    r=csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in r:\n        length[row['Geneid']]=float(row['Length'])\n        biotype[row['Geneid']]=row['gene_biotype']\n# stream count matrix, compute total and mean for protein_coding only\nwith open('inputs/BatchCorrectedReadCounts_Zenodo.csv', newline='') as f:\n    r=csv.DictReader(f)\n    headers=r.fieldnames\n    cols=[i for i,h in enumerate(headers) if h in cd14]\n    print('cd14 cols found', len(cols))\n    totals=[]; means=[]; lens=[]; genes=[]\n    for row in r:\n        gene=row[headers[0]]\n        if biotype.get(gene)=='protein_coding':\n            s=0.0\n            for i in cols:\n                val=row[headers[i]]\n                s += float(val)\n            if s>=10:\n                n=len(cols)\n                totals.append(s)\n                means.append(s/n)\n                lens.append(length[gene])\n                genes.append(gene)\nprint('eligible', len(totals))\n# Pearson pure\nn=len(lens)\nmx=sum(lens)/n; my=sum(means)/n\nsxy=sum((lens[i]-mx)*(means[i]-my) for i in range(n))\nsxx=sum((lens[i]-mx)**2 for i in range(n))\nsyy=sum((means[i]-my)**2 for i in range(n))\nr=sxy/math.sqrt(sxx*syy)\nprint('r pure', repr(r))\nprint('meanx', mx, 'meany', my)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"eligible 16096\nr pure 0.0158158302058725\nmeanx 5822.9571322067595 meany 795.3160897305582\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pandas as pd, numpy as np\nfrom scipy.stats import pearsonr\nsamp=pd.read_csv('inputs/Sample_annotated_Zenodo.csv')\ncd14_samples=samp.loc[samp['celltype']=='CD14','sample'].tolist()\nmeta=pd.read_csv('inputs/GeneMetaInfo_Zenodo.csv', index_col=0)\ncounts=pd.read_csv('inputs/BatchCorrectedReadCounts_Zenodo.csv', index_col=0)\ncd14=counts[cd14_samples]\ntotal_all=counts.sum(axis=1)\ntotal_cd14=cd14.sum(axis=1)\nmean_cd14=cd14.mean(axis=1)\nlength=meta['Length'].reindex(counts.index)\nbio=meta['gene_biotype'].reindex(counts.index)\nfor label, mask in [\n ('cd14_threshold', bio.eq('protein_coding') & (total_cd14>=10)),\n ('all_threshold', bio.eq('protein_coding') & (total_all>=10)),\n ('cd14_mean>=10', bio.eq('protein_coding') & (mean_cd14>=10)),\n ('all_threshold_mean_cd14', bio.eq('protein_coding') & (total_all>=10)),\n]:\n r=pearsonr(length[mask].to_numpy(float), mean_cd14[mask].to_numpy(float))[0]\n print(label, mask.sum(), repr(r))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
